to hibernate . If you set it to stop or terminate , you'll get an error. If Configured (for ` HibernationOptions https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/APIReference/API_HibernationOptionsRequest.html`__ ) is set to false or null , the InstanceInterruptionBehavior parameter is automatically set to terminate . You can also set it to stop or hibernate . For more information, see Interruption behavior in the Amazon EC2 User Guide . Possible values: • hibernate • stop • terminate Shorthand Syntax: MarketType=string,SpotOptions={MaxPrice=string,SpotInstanceType=string,BlockDurationMinutes=integer,ValidUntil=timestamp,InstanceInterruptionBehavior=string} JSON Syntax: { "MarketType": "spot"|"capacity-block"|"interruptible-capacity-reservation"|"on-demand", "SpotOptions": { "MaxPrice": "string", "SpotInstanceType": "one-time"|"persistent", "BlockDurationMinutes": integer, "ValidUntil": timestamp, "InstanceInterruptionBehavior": "hibernate"|"stop"|"terminate" } }
